module Main
import Base
import Borrow

-- Regression for a code-review finding on top of the Task-4/08 `Demo.lendBuffer`
-- clamp fix: `__borrow_demo` (the Task 3 internal read-test fixture) took its
-- raw `n` straight into `Utf8.demoPattern` with NO clamp to `borrowDemoCapacity`
-- and NO `max 0` floor, in BOTH the reference (`borrowDemoP`) and RC
-- (`borrowDemoRC`) interpreters -- unlike its sibling `Demo.lendBuffer`, which
-- was already clamped. `__borrow_demo 100000000000` would build a ~100 GB
-- byte pattern (hang/OOM) on an admitted, type-checked program: a reachable
-- denial-of-service via a single prelude call.
--
-- All four producer sites (reference `Demo.lendBuffer`, RC `Demo.lendBuffer`,
-- reference `__borrow_demo`, RC `__borrow_demo`) now route through the shared
-- `Utf8.clampBorrowDemoLen`, so `__borrow_demo` clamps to `borrowDemoCapacity`
-- (65536) exactly like `lendBuffer` (mirrors 08-foreign-lendbuffer-clamp.wok):
-- an ordinary negative `n` saturates to 0 bytes, and an astronomically large
-- `n` saturates to exactly the capacity instead of allocating `n` bytes.
main =
  let neg = 0 - 1 in
  let lenNeg = length (__borrow_demo neg) in
  let lenHuge = length (__borrow_demo 100000000000) in
  lenNeg + lenHuge
